              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "fitforaqueenclothing.com"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great to make for an instant craving for something sweet. I tossed in some shredded coconut to the hot oat mixture and topped it with white chocolate chips mixed with the peanut butter instead of chocolate chips. If I had nuts on hand it would have been a 5 star for sure! It wasn't overly sweet for me."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MRSPARKERII"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I changed this a little to suit my tastes and what I had on hand: I heated the brown sugar, honey and butter in the microwave until melted and then I stirred in the oatmeal, 1/4 C mixed salted nuts, and 1/4 C M&amp;Ms. Pressed them into a dish and chilled. They were so so good...salty and sweet. Next time, for a little texture, I will add wheat germ or ground flax.",
            "datePublished": "2009-06-04T12:43:43.050Z"
          },
          {
